<title>PORTUGAL: Significant inflation fall seen '97 -Bank/Portugal.</title>
<headline>Significant inflation fall seen '97 -Bank/Portugal.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The recent trend in prices paves the way for a drop in inflation in 1997, with significant falls expected in April and May, the Bank of Portugal said in its latest monthly report.  </p>
<p>&quot;The trend in inflation in February reinforces prospects for a significant reduction in inflation in 1997, with a significant drop seen in April and May,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Consumer prices rose 0.2 percent in February, with year-on-year inflation at 2.9 percent and average annual inflation at 3.2 percent.</p>
</text>
